      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Let's use Vieta's formulas to solve this problem. For a cubic equation of the form \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d = 0\\), Vieta's formulas tell us that:\n\n1. The sum of the roots \\(r + s + t = -\\frac{b}{a}\\)\n2. The sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time \\(rs + rt + st = \\frac{c}{a}\\)\n3. The product of the roots \\(rst = -\\frac{d}{a}\\)\n\nGiven the equation \\(x^3 - 20x^2 + 18x - 7 = 0\\), we can identify the coefficients as follows:\n- \\(a = 1\\)\n- \\(b = -20\\)\n- \\(c = 18\\)\n- \\(d = -7\\)\n\nUsing Vieta's formulas:\n1. \\(r + s + t = -\\frac{-20}{1} = 20\\)\n2. \\(rs + rt + st = \\frac{18}{1} = 18\\)\n3. \\(rst = -\\frac{-7}{1} = 7\\)\n\nWe need to find the value of \\((1 + r)(1 + s)(1 + t)\\). Expanding this expression, we get:\n\\[\n(1 + r)(1 + s)(1 + t) = 1 + r + s + t + rs + rt + st + rst\n\\]\nSubstituting the values from Vieta's formulas:\n\\[\n(1 + r)(1 + s)(1 + t) = 1 + 20 + 18 + 7 = 46\n\\]\nThus, the value of \\((1 + r)(1 + s)(1 + t)\\) is \\(\\boxed{46}\\).",
